WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.182
Your calling team is ready.

00:00:02.182 --> 00:00:03.665
But the list has run out.

00:00:03.665 --> 00:00:07.741
And somewhere on your computer are years of
contacts.

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:10.187
Scattered across dozens of spreadsheets.

00:00:10.187 --> 00:00:11.447
Who has already been called?

00:00:11.447 --> 00:00:12.411
Who is a customer?

00:00:12.411 --> 00:00:15.450
And which data are you paying for again?

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.022
Let's put it to the test.

00:00:19.022 --> 00:00:22.945
Ten real Excel files from an old sales archive.

00:00:22.945 --> 00:00:25.313
Together, almost thirty thousand rows.

00:00:25.313 --> 00:00:28.718
Customer details are concealed in this
recording.

00:00:28.718 --> 00:00:31.900
The counts come from the actual processing.

00:00:33.408 --> 00:00:37.493
In BelgoBase, select the files and start the
analysis.

00:00:37.493 --> 00:00:40.790
The original files are preserved.

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:46.165
Data is merged while notes and source
information are retained.

00:00:46.165 --> 00:00:50.608
Anything that cannot be reliably classified goes
to review.

00:00:52.117 --> 00:00:53.834
Here is the result.

00:00:53.834 --> 00:00:57.349
Over ten thousand records with calling
information.

00:00:57.349 --> 00:01:00.456
Almost six thousand without calling information.

00:01:00.456 --> 00:01:03.400
And a separate group to review.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:07.815
You can immediately see which data you can still
use.

00:01:07.815 --> 00:01:12.067
Here, we treat records without notes as not yet
called.

00:01:13.575 --> 00:01:17.056
Next, the assistant examines the old calling
notes.

00:01:17.056 --> 00:01:20.464
In this trial, it identifies customers and
appointments.

00:01:20.464 --> 00:01:23.292
But many notes remain unclear.

00:01:23.292 --> 00:01:27.861
The proposed profile currently produces no
priority selection.

00:01:27.861 --> 00:01:30.327
That needs your review first.

00:01:30.327 --> 00:01:34.025
It also shows where your data still falls short.

00:01:35.533 --> 00:01:40.590
Once your selection is right, you can enrich
missing contact details.

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:42.586
Using the existing phone-number finder.

00:01:42.586 --> 00:01:44.848
First, you see the cost estimate.

00:01:44.848 --> 00:01:47.908
The search starts only after your confirmation.

00:01:47.908 --> 00:01:52.033
An existing number has not automatically been
reverified.

00:01:53.533 --> 00:01:59.836
Export a compact calling list and include new
calling results

00:01:59.836 --> 00:02:01.097
in a later analysis.

00:02:01.097 --> 00:02:04.137
Build on what your team already knows.

00:02:04.137 --> 00:02:10.366
For a calling team, sales agency or business
wanting to reach

00:02:10.366 --> 00:02:11.033
a focused target audience.

00:02:12.533 --> 00:02:17.217
From scattered files to a clear next step.

00:02:17.217 --> 00:02:18.973
Keep what has value.

00:02:18.973 --> 00:02:21.315
Review what is uncertain.

00:02:21.315 --> 00:02:25.339
Focus your attention on contacts that fit your
business.

00:02:25.339 --> 00:02:26.583
That is BelgoBase.
